      <h2 id="virt-about-instance-types_virt-creating-vms-from-instance-types" class="group scroll-mt-20">About instance types<a href="#virt-about-instance-types_virt-creating-vms-from-instance-types" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">An instance type is a reusable object where you can define resources and characteristics to apply to new VMs. You can define custom instance types or use the variety that are included when you install OpenShift Virtualization.</p>
      <p>To create a new instance type, you must first create a manifest, either manually or by using the <code>virtctl</code> CLI tool. You then create the instance type object by applying the manifest to your cluster.</p>
